course: dictionary
lesson: 2210
title: Countryside
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The countryside is land outside towns and cities. It has fields, farms, woods, hills and small villages. When you meet this word, look at the words around it for clues. «Living far from friends, for example in the countryside, can be lonely» tells you the countryside is a place far from other people and towns.
explain: Stories often set adventures there. A walk through the countryside might pass a farm, a wood and a hill. Geography lessons compare the countryside with towns and cities, which is called rural versus urban.
explain: Staying safe in the countryside matters. The Countryside Code asks you to close gates, keep dogs on leads near animals, take your litter home and stay on paths. «Horses startle at sudden noise, cows protect their calves from dogs, and a bull can be very dangerous» shows why these rules exist.
fact: The countryside is land outside towns and cities.
fact: The countryside has fields, farms, woods, hills and small villages.
fact: Rural means to do with the countryside, and urban means to do with towns and cities.
fact: The Countryside Code says: close gates, keep dogs on leads near animals, take litter home and stay on paths.
fact: The muntjac is a small deer from China that escaped from parks into the English countryside about a hundred years ago.
exercise: What is the countryside? | *Land outside towns and cities, with fields, farms and woods | A kind of sea animal | The inside of a large building | A busy shopping street in a city
exercise: The Countryside Code says to keep dogs on leads near animals. Why? | Dogs need a new name | *To keep the animals safe and calm | Leads are for walking in the rain | Animals like to be chased
exercise: In geography, what does rural mean? | To do with the sea | To do with the sky | *To do with the countryside | To do with towns and cities
test: Which of these is NOT found in the countryside? | *Skyscrapers | Fields | Farms | Hills
test: Which pair is compared in geography lessons? | Mountains and deserts | Sea and sky | *Countryside and towns | Rivers and lakes
exam: A sign says «Please close the gate» in the countryside. Why? | To let the bull out | To make the field bigger | *So animals such as cows and horses stay safe and do not wander off | To make the grass grow faster
